{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/633934-meditation-humanity","id":633934,"title":"Meditation & Humanity ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-20T16:27:52-07:00","id":633934,"title":"Meditation & Humanity ?","content":"Successful daily meditation can help with mortals maintain Integrity, but would successful daily meditation help a Vampire maintain Humanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T16:39:04-07:00","id":633961,"title":"","content":"That's actually an interesting thought (sorry, dealing with idiots all day, actual insight is a welcome breath of fresh air!).<br /> <br /> On the one hand, it helps mortals maintain Integrity because it does things like lower anxiety, allow greater integration of experiences and feelings with the self, as well as potentially representing reconnecting with ones spiritual side, providing greater mental resources and resilience. However, with vampires, their Humanity measures how well they ape humanity, as well as maintain control of the Beast within.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Going to have to think about this. At the very least it'd probably <i>work</i> differently...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T16:58:16-07:00","id":633979,"title":"","content":"I would rule no, because Detatchment rolls are based on the Humanity level of the Breaking Point, not on Resolve + Composure. However, I would allow Meditation to help a vampire resist Frenzy, since that is a Resolve + Composure roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T19:51:10-07:00","id":634179,"title":"","content":"Okay, I had given this a little thought and came up with this.<br /> Imagine two Vampire monks separate from each other off in monasteries, both dealing with their curse in a similar manner, one that happens to comes naturally to monks; meditating. our first monk is meditating on silence, the meaning of life, humanity, the divine the same this he meditated on in life. until he's hungry then when an opportunity stumbles his Beast stirs and he kills again. frenzy and breaking point/Humanity drop (while as likely as any other who dances the road to damnation.)<br /> <br /> Our Second monk spends his meditative time searching with in himself for the beast, a voice in his mind that's not his own, driving him to hunt feed and kill. testing and probing these supernatural urges our monk can better resist frenzy, better ride the wave should he choose and perhaps come to an equilibrium with his Beast and his Humanity. This is the most basic philosophy of The Ordo Dracul. Study thy self, better thy self. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T20:16:39-07:00","id":634213,"title":"","content":"I think touchstones are the humanity equivalent to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T04:11:56-07:00","id":634438,"title":"","content":"I agree that it would make more sense for meditation to help with frenzy rolls and interacting with a touchstone to help with breaking points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T05:58:02-07:00","id":634485,"title":"","content":"I'd say yes. Sanctified wouldn't be able to keep their Humanity at 5 (required for using high levels of Theban Sorcery) by pursuing their God given mandate to inflict random acts of sadism on humans if their nightly prayers and devotions didn't really bolster them for the eminent breaking points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:46:21-07:00","id":634725,"title":"","content":"I see no reason not to, though probably with penalties on the Meditation roll of a newly Embraced until realization of what the Damned need to meditate &quot;about&quot;. And that doesn't preclude the possibility of Meditation also helping with Frenzy. I don't see the relation between Breaking Points and Resolve + Composure as being relevant in this. Why meditating about what it means to be human or to pretend it shouldn't help with keeping Humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:56:41-07:00","id":634734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/633934-meditation-humanity?p=634485#post634485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say yes. Sanctified wouldn't be able to keep their Humanity at 5 (required for using high levels of Theban Sorcery) by pursuing their God given mandate to inflict random acts of sadism on humans if their nightly prayers and devotions didn't really bolster them for the eminent breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to note that the Lancea et Sanctum doesn't require random acts of violence. In fact of the samples given, many could be done without a Humanity loss at all.<br /> <br /> 'With fear, a Sanctified monster keeps the wayward children of Mother Church on the straight and narrow: teenagers are terrified into maintaining their virginity by the monsters who hunt at Lovers\u2019 Leap; an abusive priest is fed on, and then driven to suicide; a family is frightened into staying with the church by nightmares and supernatural portents. With temptations, the monsters weed out the weak: A vampire plays on the deep-seated doubts of a nun, driving her to experimentation and addiction, then to prostitution and finally to homelessness and death; a televangelist is given the opportunity to embezzle funds from the Rwandan Orphanage Appeal; a student Bible-group leader is lured to his doom by a beautiful, dark woman. '<br /> <br /> Temptation and fear are what they use against the flock. You could do all of these and not drop lower than 8 or 7 depending on whether or not the abusive priest was fed on willingly or not.<br /> <br /> They reserve violence for those persecuting the church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:21:00-07:00","id":634829,"title":"","content":"The question, to me, is why would meditation help Humanity? Humanity isn't Integrity. It's one's ability to relate to and mimic humans. I think that benefiting your Humanity by avoiding humans and being alone (a breaking point if it goes on long enough) makes no sense at all. If you could do that, then it wouldn't be a breaking point to avoid human contact. You could just meditate daily to offset it.<br /> <br /> No, the only way to benefit your Humanity is to be around humans and try to understand them and remember what it was like to be them. At least, that's my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T19:10:04-07:00","id":635320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/633934-meditation-humanity?p=634829#post634829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question, to me, is why would meditation help Humanity? Humanity isn't Integrity. It's one's ability to relate to and mimic humans. I think that benefiting your Humanity by avoiding humans and being alone (a breaking point if it goes on long enough) makes no sense at all. If you could do that, then it wouldn't be a breaking point to avoid human contact. You could just meditate daily to offset it.<br /> <br /> No, the only way to benefit your Humanity is to be around humans and try to understand them and remember what it was like to be them. At least, that's my interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought would be that Meditation could help the Vampire with the Understanding. Just always struck me as odd that there were no internal actions a vampire could make in effort to remain humane.<br /> <br /> I am not looking to do away with Touchstones, I was simply looking for a more internalized alternative.<br /> <br /> Always seemed strange to me that the dice pool rolled for either maintaining or losing Humanity did not take into account the individual Vampire's own determination or mental fortitude in efforts to remain humane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T19:20:14-07:00","id":635321,"title":"","content":"I think that's covered in gaining Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T05:28:00-07:00","id":635659,"title":"","content":"Okay, meditation. If you successfully meditate before casting Theban Sorcery, you get a bonus. That is the <i>only</i> listed benefit in Requiem 2e for meditation. Unlike Requiem 1e, you don't necessarily have to reference the core World of Darkness book, the new book is entirely self contained. So, I have to question if the intent is to let the vampires have access to the standard benefits of meditation, let alone the Meditative Mind merit. Vampires don't degenerate, they suffer detachment. The +3 to Resolve+Composure is restricted to &quot;things of the world that would shake her foundation.&quot; That's directly related to the themes of the Call of Cthulhu-like mortal games and how Integrity works, and frenzy isn't shaking your foundation, its blind rage. Plus, +3 bonus for 2 exp on such a major part of vampirism is huge, and I don't think that's intended - I'd sooner think it more apprioriate to apply the bonus to checks against detachment than frenzy.<br /> <br /> Now, its easy enough to adapt the original rules for vampire, but I have to question if its thematically appropriate. If it was, I imagine it'd be touched on in the rules, since meditation is actually a fairly big part of the two religious covenants, and doubly so for the Ordo Dracul as well. But its not.<br /> <br /> The original meditation rules (and the Meditative Mind merit) are focused towards Integrity. Hacking it so that it maintains Humanity against falling is questionable; using it to reflect Coil-like benefits of controlled frenzy is, in my opinion, inappropriate for the game. That's why we have the Fighting style and the Coils!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-22-2015, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T12:47:42-07:00","id":636194,"title":"","content":"Allowing Meditation after or during a significant interaction with mortals, like a party or something without hunting or being involved with anything related to the Requiem proper, would be actually a thing to reinforce the theme. You have one more reason to try and mingle with the Cattle. Of course, do it at your own risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}